# NOTE: dist/ is intentionally NOT ignored (unlike most Vite projects). This app supports
# a notebook/Git-folder deploy route with no local npm/node available -- if dist/ isn't
# committed, a fresh Git folder clone has no way to produce it. Run `npm run build` and
# commit the updated frontend/dist/ after any change to frontend/src/.

# NOTE: package-lock.json IS committed (unlike uv.lock at the repo root -- see that
# file's own note). This project was originally developed on a machine whose npm is
# globally configured to resolve packages through a Databricks-internal registry proxy
# (npm-proxy.dev.databricks.com), which mirrors the public npm registry 1:1 (identical
# package tarball paths/hashes -- npm registry proxies of this kind always do, unlike
# PyPI's split index-vs-file-host architecture). The committed lockfile has its registry
# URLs rewritten to the real public registry (registry.npmjs.org) so it resolves outside
# Databricks' network too. If you regenerate this file on a similarly-configured
# machine, re-run: sed -i '' 's|https://npm-proxy\.dev\.databricks\.com/|https://registry.npmjs.org/|g' package-lock.json
# and confirm `npm ci` still succeeds before committing.

